        "filename": "Nyakuer Rambang and son Wiyual Makuach fled conflict in Nassir, Upper Nile State, now living in Kule Refugee Camp, Gambella, Ethiopia (14950287898).jpg",
        "caption": "Wiyual is Nyakuer Rambang's only remaining son, as her other three sons were killed in conflict or trying to escape the fighting. \n'If the situation is calm in South Sudan I will return, but if not, I will stay here until the problem gets better. Even in the conflict before independence I was okay. This war has cost thousands of lives. Even the last war did not cause so many people to die. It is very difficult for me because I lost my sons.'\n\nPhoto: Oxfam/Aimee Brown",
        "alt": "Wiyual is Nyakuer Rambang's only remaining son, as her other three sons were killed in conflict or trying to escape the fighting. \n'If the situation is calm in South Sudan I will return, but if not, I will stay here until the problem gets better. Even in the conflict before independence I was okay. This war has cost thousands of lives. Even the last war did not cause so many people to die. It is very difficult for me because I lost my sons.'\n\nPhoto: Oxfam/Aimee Brown",
